{
  "why": "The drop tables of the standard Normal / Special / Rare equipment that monsters of the Mega-Dungeon drop without limit (1.55.0, builder GEAR). They are data so the owner or a pack can retune the drops without a mod update (a data pack file of the same path replaces this one; /reload applies it). The three base chances, the shift per floor and the Looting bonus are NOT here: they are server config keys (nusmp-labyrinth-mega-gear-server.toml) because they are the knobs of one server, while this file holds the SHAPES: how the grade mix moves with depth, what each grade is made of, which slots are likely. Every item id is a vanilla item on purpose: standard gear is ordinary items stamped with the nusmp:gear_grade component, never relics, so no relic ledger or world limit ever applies to it (docs/labyrinth/mega_gear.md).",

  "curve": {
    "why": "Multiplier of each grade's base chance along the depth progress x = floorShift * (threat - 1), clamped to 0..1 (x = 1 at floor 51 with the default shift). With the default bases 0.05 / 0.015 / 0.004 the three multiplied chances add up to about 0.069 at every depth (within 6 percent), so going deeper MOVES weight from Normal to Special and Rare instead of adding drops: Normal falls to 0.40, Special peaks at x = 0.5 (about floor 26) and eases back to 1.40, Rare keeps rising to 6.",
    "normal":  [[0.0, 1.0], [0.5, 0.64], [1.0, 0.40]],
    "special": [[0.0, 1.0], [0.5, 1.95], [1.0, 1.40]],
    "rare":    [[0.0, 1.0], [0.5, 2.40], [1.0, 6.00]]
  },

  "caps": {
    "why": "Ceilings that hold whatever the config asks for: no grade drops on more than the stated share of kills, and the three together never pass total. They keep a mistyped config (normalChance 5) from turning every kill into a shower of gear.",
    "normal": 0.30,
    "special": 0.20,
    "rare": 0.15,
    "total": 0.50
  },

  "slotWeights": {
    "why": "How likely each kind of piece is when a drop is decided. They add up to 100 so each reads as a percent: half the drops are armour (four pieces of 13), about four in ten are weapons, one in eleven a shield. A slot a grade has no base item for is simply never rolled for that grade.",
    "sword": 18, "axe": 8, "bow": 8, "crossbow": 5, "shield": 9,
    "helmet": 13, "chestplate": 13, "leggings": 13, "boots": 13
  },

